- Use targeted edits; never rewrite a whole file for a small change.
- Run only the tests for the file you changed (yarn test <path>) plus
  yarn typecheck. Run full yarn validate once at the end of a task.
- If the same error persists after two attempts, stop and tell me what you tried.
- Do not browse the web or fetch docs unless I ask; use package.json and the repo.
- Keep plans to 10 lines and summaries to 10 lines. Ask questions only if blocked.

# Testing conventions

- Test behavior, not implementation. Query by role, label, or text — never by testID.
- Every screen tests loading, error, empty, and populated states.
- All network calls are mocked with typed MSW handlers (response bodies typed from app types via `z.infer` or generated types).
- No whole-screen snapshot tests.
- No `any` in tests (enforced by `@typescript-eslint/no-explicit-any`).
- Every bug fix ships with a regression test.
- A test must fail if the feature it covers is broken.
- When a new feature folder is added, it must be added to `collectCoverageFrom` in `jest.config.js` in the same PR, together with tests.
